{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A4mvnb5W27SzesFhQAwZLV","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel05.4\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel05.4 — md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum\"\n     3→release: rel05.4\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel05.4-uc001-md5sum\n     7→  - rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum\n     8→  - rel05.4-uc003-sha256sum\n     9→  - rel05.4-uc004-sha512sum\n    10→  - prd030-md5sum R1\n    11→  - prd030-md5sum R2\n    12→  - prd031-sha1sum R1\n    13→  - prd031-sha1sum R2\n    14→  - prd032-sha256sum R1\n    15→  - prd032-sha256sum R2\n    16→  - prd033-sha512sum R1\n    17→  - prd033-sha512sum R2\n    18→\n    19→preconditions:\n    20→  - ./bin/md5sum, ./bin/sha1sum, ./bin/sha256sum, and ./bin/sha512sum exist (built via mage build).\n    21→  - Reference binaries gmd5sum, gsha1sum, gsha256sum, and gsha512sum are installed via Homebrew (coreutils) and on PATH.\n    22→  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/md5sum/... ./cmd/sha1sum/... ./cmd/sha256sum/... ./cmd/sha512sum/... which invoke RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n    23→  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n    24→  - No normalization is applied; all outputs are compared byte-for-byte.\n    25→  - Test setup creates a known file (e.g. containing \"hello\\n\") and a pre-computed checksum file for check-mode tests.\n    26→\n    27→test_cases:\n    28→\n    29→  # ---- md5sum ----\n    30→\n    31→  - name: md5sum_compute_stdin\n    32→    description: Compute MD5 of stdin; output is \"HASH  -\" in GNU text format.\n    33→    inputs:\n    34→      args: []\n    35→      stdin: \"hello\\n\"\n    36→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    37→    normalization: none\n    38→    expected:\n    39→      exit_code: 0\n    40→      stdout: \"b1946ac92492d2347c6235b4d2611184  -\\n\"\n    41→      stderr: \"\"\n    42→    traces:\n    43→      - prd030-md5sum R1.1\n    44→      - prd030-md5sum R1.2\n    45→\n    46→  - name: md5sum_compute_file\n    47→    description: \"Compute MD5 of a named file. Setup: hello.txt contains 'hello\\\\n'.\"\n    48→    inputs:\n    49→      args: [\"hello.txt\"]\n    50→      stdin: null\n    51→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    52→    normalization: none\n    53→    expected:\n    54→      exit_code: 0\n    55→      stdout: \"b1946ac92492d2347c6235b4d2611184  hello.txt\\n\"\n    56→      stderr: \"\"\n    57→    traces:\n    58→      - prd030-md5sum R1.1\n    59→\n    60→  - name: md5sum_binary_mode\n    61→    description: \"-b uses asterisk format: 'HASH *FILENAME'.\"\n    62→    inputs:\n    63→      args: [\"-b\", \"hello.txt\"]\n    64→      stdin: null\n    65→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    66→    normalization: none\n    67→    expected:\n    68→      exit_code: 0\n    69→      stdout: \"b1946ac92492d2347c6235b4d2611184 *hello.txt\\n\"\n    70→      stderr: \"\"\n    71→    traces:\n    72→      - prd030-md5sum R3.1\n    73→\n    74→  - name: md5sum_tag_format\n    75→    description: \"--tag uses BSD format: 'MD5 (FILENAME) = HASH'.\"\n    76→    inputs:\n    77→      args: [\"--tag\", \"hello.txt\"]\n    78→      stdin: null\n    79→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    80→    normalization: none\n    81→    expected:\n    82→      exit_code: 0\n    83→      stdout: \"MD5 (hello.txt) = b1946ac92492d2347c6235b4d2611184\\n\"\n    84→      stderr: \"\"\n    85→    traces:\n    86→      - prd030-md5sum R1.3\n    87→\n    88→  - name: md5sum_check_valid\n    89→    description: \"--check on a valid checksum file exits 0 and prints OK. Setup: checksums.md5 contains the correct hash for hello.txt.\"\n    90→    inputs:\n    91→      args: [\"--check\", \"checksums.md5\"]\n    92→      stdin: null\n    93→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    94→    normalization: none\n    95→    expected:\n    96→      exit_code: 0\n    97→      stdout: \"hello.txt: OK\\n\"\n    98→      stderr: \"\"\n    99→    traces:\n   100→      - prd030-md5sum R2.1\n   101→      - prd030-md5sum R2.2\n   102→\n   103→  - name: md5sum_check_failure\n   104→    description: \"--check on a file with wrong hash exits 1 and prints FAILED. Setup: bad.md5 contains an incorrect hash for hello.txt.\"\n   105→    inputs:\n   106→      args: [\"--check\", \"bad.md5\"]\n   107→      stdin: null\n   108→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   109→    normalization: none\n   110→    expected:\n   111→      exit_code: 1\n   112→      stdout: \"hello.txt: FAILED\\n\"\n   113→      stderr_contains: \"WARNING\"\n   114→    traces:\n   115→      - prd030-md5sum R2.2\n   116→\n   117→  # ---- sha1sum ----\n   118→\n   119→  - name: sha1sum_compute_stdin\n   120→    description: Compute SHA-1 of stdin.\n   121→    inputs:\n   122→      args: []\n   123→      stdin: \"hello\\n\"\n   124→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   125→    normalization: none\n   126→    expected:\n   127→      exit_code: 0\n   128→      stdout: \"f572d396fae9206628714fb2ce00f72e94f2258f  -\\n\"\n   129→      stderr: \"\"\n   130→    traces:\n   131→      - prd031-sha1sum R1.1\n   132→      - prd031-sha1sum R1.2\n   133→\n   134→  - name: sha1sum_check_valid\n   135→    description: \"--check on a valid SHA-1 checksum file exits 0.\"\n   136→    inputs:\n   137→      args: [\"--check\", \"checksums.sha1\"]\n   138→      stdin: null\n   139→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   140→    normalization: none\n   141→    expected:\n   142→      exit_code: 0\n   143→      stdout: \"hello.txt: OK\\n\"\n   144→      stderr: \"\"\n   145→    traces:\n   146→      - prd031-sha1sum R2.1\n   147→      - prd031-sha1sum R2.2\n   148→\n   149→  - name: sha1sum_tag_format\n   150→    description: \"--tag uses BSD format: 'SHA1 (FILENAME) = HASH'.\"\n   151→    inputs:\n   152→      args: [\"--tag\", \"hello.txt\"]\n   153→      stdin: null\n   154→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   155→    normalization: none\n   156→    expected:\n   157→      exit_code: 0\n   158→      stdout: \"SHA1 (hello.txt) = f572d396fae9206628714fb2ce00f72e94f2258f\\n\"\n   159→    